摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dsh 宿主插件——经 webserver 钩子向页面注入旧内核浏览器 polyfill。","id":"gh:1333628907","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-host-web-compat","slug":"kelai141/dsh-host-web-compat","topics":["dsh-plugin","polyfill"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh 宿主插件——经 webserver 钩子向页面注入旧内核浏览器 polyfill。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-host-web-compat"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"🌐 中文说明 / 中文 README"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **DeepSeek Harness × Android ecosystem** · dsh-mobile-apk (shell APK) · dsh-shell-termux (shell) ·"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" dsh-client-ui-responsive (mobile UI)"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Host plugin for DeepSeek Harness that injects\nlegacy-browser polyfills into every served page via th"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"e webserver `tapIndex` hook, and bridges the\nshell APK's directory picker and path-open channels."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Background"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Older kernels (MuMu's bundled browser, older WebViews) lack APIs the host page calls directly:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- missing `AbortSignal.any()` breaks the workspace directory picker's concurrent RPC cancellation;\n-"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" missing `Promise.withResolvers()` breaks the host boot-ready tail script, failing the plugin tree;\n"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"- missing global `Iterator` (Chrome 122+) makes upstream 0.1.5 client bundles (documentpreview and\no"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"thers) throw `Iterator is not defined` at import time (\"Failed to load plugins\")."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The plugin injects idempotent polyfills at the HTML level — no browser-side changes needed."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**1. Install** — package into the profile's node_modules."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**2. Mount** — in the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**3. Restart** the service; the picker works again in old kernels."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Polyfills injected"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| API | condition | note |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| `AbortSignal.any` | missing | Chrome 116+ / Node 20.3+ |\n| `AbortSignal.timeout` | missing | Chrom"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"e 103+ / Node 17.3+ |\n| `structuredClone` | missing | Chrome 98+ / Node 17+ |\n| `Object.hasOwn` | mi"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ssing | Chrome 93+ / Safari 15.4+ |\n| `Array.prototype.at` | missing | Chrome 92+ |\n| `String.protot"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"ype.replaceAll` | missing | Chrome 85+ |\n| `crypto.randomUUID` | missing | Chrome 92+, secure contex"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"t required |\n| `Promise.withResolvers` | missing | Chrome 119+; the host boot-ready tail depends on "},{"id":"p17s6","text":"it |\n| global `Iterator` + iterator helpers | missing | Chrome 122+ (map/filter/take/drop/flatMap/to"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"Array/forEach/some/every/find/reduce + `Iterator.from`) |\n| `Object.groupBy` / `Map.groupBy` | missi"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"ng | Chrome 117+ |\n| `Set.prototype` set methods | missing | Chrome 122+ (union/intersection/differe"},{"id":"p17s9","text":"nce/symmetricDifference/isSubsetOf/isSupersetOf/isDisjointFrom) |\n| `Array.fromAsync` | missing | Ch"},{"id":"p17s10","text":"icDifference/isSubsetOf/isSupersetOf/isDisjointFrom) |\n| `Array.fromAsync` | missing | Chrome 121+ |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Idempotent: skipped when already present. Every snippet shares **one** `<script>` element, so each\no"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ne must end on a complete statement (see Development constraints)."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Other injections"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- Directory-picker bridge (`__dshBridge` plus the `/api/android/dir-pick/*` polling endpoints that\nr"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"eturn real SAF paths);\n- open-path (`window.__dshOpenPath`: chat mentions and tool-row paths into th"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"e shell chooser) —\n0.14 makes resolution session-scoped (relative paths resolve against the active s"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"ession cwd);\n- theme bridge (`__dshThemeBridge`: system light/dark into page theme variables);\n- age"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"nt tool-row path recognition — 0.14 keys on DOM facts (not CSS-module class names) when\nclicking an "},{"id":"p20s6","text":"absolute path in a tool row hands it to the shell chooser;\n- clipboard fallback (2026-10-03): a glob"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"al wrapper over `navigator.clipboard.writeText`. Android\nWebView denies the async Clipboard API (`No"},{"id":"p20s8","text":"tAllowedError: Write permission denied`; WebView has no\npermission prompt), and upstream `writeClipb"},{"id":"p20s9","text":"oard` returns false from its `catch` — it only falls\nback to `execCommand('copy')` when the API is *"},{"id":"p20s10","text":"absent* — so every copy button wrote nothing and\nshowed nothing. The wrapper falls back to the shell"},{"id":"p20s11","text":" bridge `window.androidBridge.copyText`\n(ClipboardManager), then to `execCommand('copy')`, and emits"},{"id":"p20s12","text":" one plain-language notice when all\nthree fail. Patching the API instead of each caller covers CodeB"},{"id":"p20s13","text":"lock / MessageIconActions /\nTerminalBlock / HoverCard / user-questions / trajectory and third-party "},{"id":"p20s14","text":"plugins, which all read\nthe API at click time;\n- boot watchdog: 40s stuck diagnostics plus the three"},{"id":"p20s15","text":" contract lines the shell APK parses by\nfield position (`[dsh-boot-stall]` stuck, `[dsh-boot-ready]`"},{"id":"p20s16","text":" really rendered,\n`[dsh-boot-failed]` client plugin tree failed) — see Boot diagnostics contract."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Boot diagnostics contract"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The watchdog reports on the `console.error` channel. The shell APK matches the line prefix and then\n"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"reads the remaining fields **by position**, so the field order below is part of the interface:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| line | meaning | fields after the prefix |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| `[dsh-boot-stall] dsh-boot-diag source=page-stall ...` | 40s without a render | `pageSideRuntime=<"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"folded JSON> detail=<folded k=v>` |\n| `[dsh-boot-ready] dsh-boot-diag source=page-ready ...` | `#roo"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"t` rendered **and** the boot page is gone | `pageSideRuntime=<folded JSON>` |\n| `[dsh-boot-failed] d"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"sh-boot-diag source=page-plugin-fail ...` | client plugin tree failed | `detail=reason=<first line, "},{"id":"p24s5","text":"200 chars> takenMs=<ms> failedCount=<N> rendered=<bool>`, `failedIds=<comma list or ->`, `pageSideRu"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"ntime=<folded JSON, last>` |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"`failedIds` keeps only items that look like a loader entry id\n(`/^[@A-Za-z0-9][@A-Za-z0-9._\\/-]*$/`,"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" at most 120 characters), at most 8 items, unquoted and\nspace-free; `-` when none is readable. It si"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ts **before** `pageSideRuntime` because `fold`\ntruncates at 2048 characters and a truncated JSON tai"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"l cannot be parsed at all."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Readiness is `rendered() && !bootPagePresent()`. A failed client plugin tree renders a boot page\ntha"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"t still gives `#root` children, so the old `rendered()`-only criterion reported it as ready: the\nshe"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ll stopped its stall timer and the failure stayed silent. The failure line is published from two\nide"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"mpotent trigger points — the `MutationObserver` callback (2s debounce) and every `readyWatch`\ntick, "},{"id":"p26s5","text":"which covers a failure page that reached its final state before the observer was installed.\n`pending"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"Boot()` is unchanged, so a failure page deliberately does **not** raise the 40s overlay: it\nexits th"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"rough `[dsh-boot-failed]` instead."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Development constraints"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Snippets live in the `POLYFILLS` array; the assembly rule is `POLYFILL_SCRIPT_BODY` in\n`lib/index.js"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ippets live in the `POLYFILLS` array; the assembly rule is `POLYFILL_SCRIPT_BODY` in\n`lib/index.js`:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- **Every snippet must end with `;` or `}`.** All snippets share one `<script>` element, and a\nsingl"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"e syntax error makes the parser reject the whole element: the page then behaves as if no\npolyfill ex"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"isted while the served HTML still contains the snippet text (measured 2026-09-10 — the\nSet-methods I"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"IFE ended with `})()` against the next snippet's `if (`, so WebView 110 reported\n`Iterator is not de"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"fined` at import time).\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
